 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Opt-in `batch1d_iter(..., copy_arrays=False)` for independently owned,
+  read-only, C-contiguous float64 NumPy frames. Streaming workers retain each
+  Python owner and a read guard until native integration finishes, avoiding
+  the producer's full-frame snapshot copy. Arrays and storage aliases must
+  remain unchanged while in flight. The default remains `copy_arrays=True`
+  for generators that reuse mutable decoding buffers.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Release the GIL while a streaming producer waits for queue capacity, allowing
+  native consumers to acquire NumPy read guards without deadlocking. Report
+  invalid yielded arrays and generator exceptions as failed results instead of
+  silently truncating the stream.
+
 ## [0.6.1] - 2026-10-24
 
 ### Changed
